- ly display manager 
  A lightweight, text-mode display manager (also referred to as a greeter) for Linux and BSD systems

- i3 window manager 
  Lightweight tiling window manager for X11 window system

- i3status 
  Official i3 status bar that ships with i3 out of the box 

- picom
  A lightweight, standalone compositor for X11 windowing system (used to add visual effects and fix rendering issues for window mangers that lack built-in compositing)

- kitty
  Free, open-source, GPU-accelerated terminal emulator designed for speed, extensibility, and power users who prefer keyboard-centric workflows

- neovim (nvim)
  Terminal text editor

- fastfetch
  High-performance command line tool used to view system information

- cmatrix 
  A popular, open-source terminal-based program that simulates the iconic "digital rain" falling green code effect

- neomutt 
  Terminal based email client 

- htop 
  A cross-platform, interactive process viewer

- lsusb (provided by usbutils in arch linux core repository)
   A command-line utility in Linux used to list and display information about USB buses and the devices connected to them

- browser 
  Mostly I use either Brave or Firefox, but qutebrowser is also a option 

- nautilus 
  A graphical file explorer which is mostly used for gnome but i use it, as it looks good

- code 
  Visual Studio Code is a free, open-source, and lightweight code editor ("vs code oss" from the official archlinux repository)
